s/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option        | Meaning                                      | Typical use     |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `dragAndDrop` | Enables drag and drop plus its policy hooks. | Editable trees. |","table":"table-0"},"455":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#41","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option     | Meaning                                  | Typical use                |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `renaming` | Enables inline rename plus policy hooks. | Rename-in-place workflows. |","table":"table-0"},"456":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#42","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option        | Meaning                                              | Typical use                                    |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `composition` | Context-menu behavior flags and lifecycle callbacks. | Choose the menu trigger and button visibility. |","table":"table-0"},"457":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#43","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option      | Meaning                         | Typical use                                                       |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gitStatus` | Built-in Git-style row signals. | Added, modified, deleted, ignored, renamed, and untracked states. |","table":"table-0"},"458":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#44","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option  | Meaning                                         | Typical use                                                   |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `icons` | Built-in icon set or icon configuration object. | Set selection, color mode, remaps, or sprite-sheet extension. |","table":"table-0"},"459":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#45","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option   | Meaning                             | Typical use                                                      |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `labels` | User-visible text the tree renders. | Localize the search placeholder, accessible names, and tooltips. |","table":"table-0"},"460":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#46","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option                | Meaning                             | Typical use                                              |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `renderRowDecoration` | Custom non-Git row signal renderer. | Generated-file badges, remote markers, validation hints. |","table":"table-0"},"461":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#47","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option    | Meaning                                  | Typical use                               |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `density` | Density preset or custom spacing factor. | Tune row height and spacing in one place. |","table":"table-0"},"462":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#48","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option       | Meaning                       | Typical use                                       |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `itemHeight` | Explicit row-height override. | Row height that doesn't match a `density` preset. |","table":"table-0"},"463":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#49","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option     | Meaning                                         | Typical use                 |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `overscan` | Extra rows rendered outside the visible window. | Smooth scrolling tradeoffs. |","table":"table-0"},"464":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#50","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option                   | Meaning                                                              | Typical use                                               |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `initialVisibleRowCount` | Optional first-render row budget before the browser measures height. | Tune first-render work without pinning steady-state size. |","table":"table-0"},"465":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#51","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#shared-option-groups","content":"| Option          | Meaning                                                   | Typical use                         |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `stickyFolders` | Pins the ancestor folders of the top row while scrolling. | Keep context visible in deep trees. |","table":"table-0"},"466":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#52","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#tree-shape-options","content":"The tree-shape options are `paths`, `preparedInput`, `initialExpansion`,\n`initialExpandedPaths`, `flattenEmptyDirectories`, and `sort`."},"467":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#53","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#tree-shape-options","content":"Use them to answer three questions:"},"468":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#54","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#tree-shape-options","content":"where the tree data comes from"},"469":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#55","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#tree-shape-options","content":"what the initial visible shape must be"},"470":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#56","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#tree-shape-options","content":"whether the client must still shape or sort the data"},"471":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#57","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#tree-shape-options","content":"For the recommended setup, read\nShape tree data for fast rendering."},"472":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#58","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#search-mode-semantics","content":"`solid-trees` supports three search modes:"},"473":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#59","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#search-mode-semantics","content":"`hide-non-matches`: shows only the matches and the ancestor chain that keeps\nthem navigable. This is the guide default."},"474":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#60","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#search-mode-semantics","content":"`collapse-non-matches`: keeps the matching paths and the ancestor chain\nvisible. It collapses unrelated branches out of the way."},"475":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#61","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#search-mode-semantics","content":"`expand-matches`: expands the matching branches into the surrounding tree\ncontext. It keeps non-matching rows visible."},"476":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#62","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#search-mode-semantics","content":"The built-in search input, `createFileTreeSearch(...)`, and the model search\nmethods all use the same search modes."},"477":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#63","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#selection-focus-and-item-handles","content":"Selection is path-based. Focus is path-based. Item handles are path-oriented\nhelpers for a known item."},"478":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#64","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#selection-focus-and-item-handles","content":"Common lookup topics are:"},"479":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#65","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#selection-focus-and-item-handles","content":"get an item by path"},"480":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#66","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#selection-focus-and-item-handles","content":"read the focused and selected state"},"481":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#67","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#selection-focus-and-item-handles","content":"focus, select, toggle, or deselect through the model or item handle"},"482":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#68","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#selection-focus-and-item-handles","content":"expand, collapse, or toggle directories through a directory handle"},"483":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#69","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#selection-focus-and-item-handles","content":"Read\nNavigate selection, focus, and search\nfor workflows. Read Solid API for the reactive\nprimitives. Read Model API for direct model\nmethods."},"484":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#70","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#interaction-and-editing-options","content":"`dragAndDrop`, `renaming`, and `composition` are the editing surfaces. They\nshare the same path-first event model. Header and context-menu content are Solid\nJSX, passed to `<FileTree>` as the `header` and `renderContextMenu` props."},"485":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#71","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#interaction-and-editing-options","content":"Read\nRename, drag, and trigger item actions\nfor the user-facing workflows that build on those options."},"486":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#72","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#appearance-and-annotation-options","content":"`gitStatus`, `icons`, and `renderRowDecoration` all affect how rows look. But\nthey do different jobs:"},"487":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#73","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#appearance-and-annotation-options","content":"`gitStatus` is the built-in Git-style signal lane"},"488":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#74","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#appearance-and-annotation-options","content":"`icons` controls icon sets, remaps, and sprite-sheet extension"},"489":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#75","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#appearance-and-annotation-options","content":"`renderRowDecoration` adds non-Git row metadata"},"490":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#76","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#appearance-and-annotation-options","content":"Page CSS is the narrow fallback when public styling surfaces are not enough. For\ndeeper lookup, read Styling and theming\nand Icons."},"491":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#77","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#scale-and-rendering-settings","content":"`initialVisibleRowCount`, `density`, `itemHeight`, and `overscan` are rendering\nknobs, not onboarding concepts. The rendered container sets the steady-state\nheight. These options only tune the first-render budget, the visual density, and\nthe virtualized row window."},"492":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#78","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#scale-and-rendering-settings","content":"For density, use the `density` keyword (`'compact' | 'default' | 'relaxed'`) or\na numeric factor. It sets both the row height and the spacing in one place.\n`<FileTree>` paints `--trees-item-height` and `--trees-density-override` for\nyou. Use `itemHeight` only when you need a row height that does not match a\npreset."},"493":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#79","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#scale-and-rendering-settings","content":"Read\nHandle large trees efficiently\nwhen scale becomes the real problem."},"494":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#80","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"`solid-trees` exposes semantic tree mutations, not DOM events. The shared\nmutation terms are:"},"495":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#81","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"`add`"},"496":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#82","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"`remove`"},"497":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#83","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"`move`"},"498":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#84","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"`batch`"},"499":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#85","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"`resetPaths`"},"500":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#86","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"`onMutation`"},"501":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#87","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"Mutation payloads stay path-first. Reset events also report whether prepared\ninput was involved. Invalidation metadata reports whether the canonical state or\nthe projected visible state changed."},"502":{"id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#88","page_id":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/shared-concepts#mutation-vocabulary","content":"Use these events to sync adjacent UI, analytics, or persistence layers. Do not\nturn them into a filesystem-sync tutorial."},"503":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"page","content":"Solid API","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api"},"504":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#0","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api","content":"createFileTree, the FileTree component, and the reactive primitives over the model."},"505":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#1","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#model-first-story","content":"Model-first story"},"506":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#2","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#createfiletree","content":"`createFileTree(...)`"},"507":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#3","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#filetree-","content":"`<FileTree />`"},"508":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#4","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#reading-tree-state-from-solid","content":"Reading tree state from Solid"},"509":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#5","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#primitives","content":"Primitives"},"510":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#6","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#writing-to-the-model-from-solid","content":"Writing to the model from Solid"},"511":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#7","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#composition-surface","content":"Composition surface"},"512":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#8","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#mutation-and-subscriptions-from-solid","content":"Mutation and subscriptions from Solid"},"513":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#9","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#appearance-boundary","content":"Appearance boundary"},"514":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#10","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api","content":"Everything lives at the package root, `solid-trees`. The Solid layer is a thin\nintegration over one imperative model, `FileTreeModel`."},"515":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#11","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#model-first-story","content":"Start with `createFileTree(options)`. Do not build a large controlled component.\nThe primitive creates one stable model for the owner's lifetime. Later option\nchanges do not reconfigure the model. Update the model through model methods\ninstead."},"516":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#12","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#model-first-story","content":"For the shared option meanings behind that call, read\nShared concepts."},"517":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#13","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#createfiletree","content":"`createFileTree(...)`:"},"518":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#14","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#createfiletree","content":"accepts the shared tree-options surface"},"519":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#15","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#createfiletree","content":"creates the model one time"},"520":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#16","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#createfiletree","content":"cleans up the model when the current reactive owner disposes (called outside\nan owner, call `cleanUp()` yourself)"},"521":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#17","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#createfiletree","content":"returns the `FileTreeModel`"},"522":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#18","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#createfiletree","content":"Use model methods when the tree changes after mount. The methods include\n`resetPaths(...)`, `setComposition(...)`, `setGitStatus(...)`, `setIcons(...)`,\n`setLabels(...)`, and the search or mutation methods."},"523":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#19","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#filetree-","content":"The Solid component renders the model into the light DOM."},"524":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#20","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#filetree-","content":"Primary props:"},"525":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#21","page_id":