s are:"},"552":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#48","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#writing-to-the-model-from-solid","content":"focus and selection methods on the model or item handles. This includes\n`scrollToPath(...)`, which reveals a path without moving DOM focus and makes\noptional model focus changes."},"553":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#49","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#writing-to-the-model-from-solid","content":"visible-tree traversal through `focusFirstItem()`, `focusLastItem()`,\n`focusNextItem()`, `focusPreviousItem()`, and `focusParentItem()`."},"554":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#50","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#writing-to-the-model-from-solid","content":"visible row inspection through `getFocusedIndex()`, `getVisibleCount()`, and\n`getVisibleRows(start, end)` when surrounding UI needs custom navigation."},"555":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#51","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#writing-to-the-model-from-solid","content":"search methods such as `setSearch(...)` and `openSearch(...)`"},"556":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#52","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#writing-to-the-model-from-solid","content":"mutation methods such as `add(...)`, `remove(...)`, `move(...)`, `batch(...)`,\nand `resetPaths(...)`"},"557":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#53","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#writing-to-the-model-from-solid","content":"runtime reconfiguration methods such as `setComposition(...)`,\n`setGitStatus(...)`, `setIcons(...)`, and `setLabels(...)`"},"558":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#54","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#writing-to-the-model-from-solid","content":"The full list is in Model API."},"559":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#55","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#composition-surface","content":"`<FileTree>` adds two composition props on top of the model:"},"560":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#56","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#composition-surface","content":"`header` for Solid-rendered header content, above the search input and rows"},"561":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#57","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#composition-surface","content":"`renderContextMenu(item, context)` for Solid-rendered context menus; providing\nit enables the menu"},"562":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#58","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#composition-surface","content":"Use `composition.contextMenu` on the model for the behavior flags (`enabled`,\n`triggerMode`, `buttonVisibility`) and the `onOpen` / `onClose` callbacks. The\nshared meaning of the composition options is in\nShared concepts."},"563":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#59","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#mutation-and-subscriptions-from-solid","content":"Use primitives and tracked getters when Solid UI needs reactive reads. Use\n`model.onMutation(...)` when you need semantic side effects. Examples are\npersistence, logging, or analytics around add, remove, move, reset, or batch\noperations."},"564":{"id":"/docs/reference/solid-api#60","page_id":"/docs/reference/solid-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/solid-api#appearance-boundary","content":"Style the host with normal host props such as `class` and `style`. For deeper\nlookup, read Styling and theming and\nIcons."},"565":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"page","content":"Styling and theming","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming"},"566":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#0","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","content":"Lookup reference for host styling, CSS variables, themeToTreeStyles, layers, and page CSS."},"567":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#1","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#styling-entry-points","content":"Styling entry points"},"568":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#2","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"CSS custom property families"},"569":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#3","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#fallback-precedence","content":"Fallback precedence"},"570":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#4","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"`themeToTreeStyles(...)`"},"571":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#5","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#scoping-and-layers","content":"Scoping and layers"},"572":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#6","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#page-resets","content":"Page resets"},"573":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#7","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#color-scheme","content":"Color scheme"},"574":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#8","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#page-css-escape-hatch","content":"Page CSS escape hatch"},"575":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#9","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#related-pages","content":"Related pages"},"576":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#10","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","content":"This page is the lookup reference for host styling, CSS-variable families,\n`themeToTreeStyles(...)`, the stylesheet layers, and page CSS."},"577":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#11","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#styling-entry-points","content":"Host styling comes first. Use normal host `class` and `style` props on\n`<FileTree model={...} />`."},"578":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#12","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#styling-entry-points","content":"Host styles own width, height, borders, background, and panel placement. CSS\nvariables control the UI inside that host."},"579":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#13","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#styling-entry-points","content":"Import the stylesheet once:"},"580":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#14","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"The tree styling surface uses variable families, not one flat list."},"581":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#15","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"Core families include:"},"582":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#16","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"panel, background, and foreground tokens"},"583":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#17","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"hover, selection, and focus tokens"},"584":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#18","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"input and search tokens"},"585":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#19","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"Git-status color tokens"},"586":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#20","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"icon color tokens for supported built-in icon sets"},"587":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#21","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#css-custom-property-families","content":"density and spacing tokens"},"588":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#22","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#fallback-precedence","content":"`solid-trees` resolves styling in this order:"},"589":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#23","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#fallback-precedence","content":"explicit override variables such as `--trees-*-override`"},"590":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#24","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#fallback-precedence","content":"`--trees-theme-*` variables from theme helpers"},"591":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#25","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#fallback-precedence","content":"library defaults"},"592":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#26","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#fallback-precedence","content":"So `themeToTreeStyles(...)` fills the middle layer. Direct overrides still win."},"593":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#27","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"`themeToTreeStyles(theme)` maps a VS Code or Shiki-style theme object into host\nstyles. It also maps the theme to the `--trees-theme-*` variables that the tree\nunderstands."},"594":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#28","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"Input shape:"},"595":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#29","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"`TreeThemeInput`"},"596":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#30","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"key fields: `type`, `colors`"},"597":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#31","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"Output shape:"},"598":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#32","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"`TreeThemeStyles`"},"599":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#33","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"keyed by CSS property names (`background-color`, not `backgroundColor`), so it\nworks directly as a Solid `style` object"},"600":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#34","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#themetotreestyles","content":"The helper covers panel colors, selection colors, focus rings, input colors, and\nGit-status colors. Explicit overrides can still replace any derived token later."},"601":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#35","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#scoping-and-layers","content":"Every rule sits in `@scope ([data-file-tree-virtualized-root])`. Header and\ncontext-menu content is excluded from the scope; it still inherits color and\nfont from the root."},"602":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#36","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#scoping-and-layers","content":"The stylesheet uses three cascade layers:\n`@layer solid-trees.structure, solid-trees.base, solid-trees.theme`."},"603":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#37","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#scoping-and-layers","content":"`solid-trees.structure` holds the virtualizer layout, row lanes, and\ntruncation mechanics. `<FileTree>` injects it itself, so trees work without\nthe stylesheet."},"604":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#38","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#scoping-and-layers","content":"`solid-trees.base` comes from `solid-trees/styles.css`."},"605":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#39","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#scoping-and-layers","content":"`solid-trees.theme` is reserved for your theme rules."},"606":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#40","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#scoping-and-layers","content":"Unlayered page CSS overrides every layer."},"607":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#41","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#page-resets","content":"The base layer starts with a reset for the tree's own controls, so element rules\nfrom layers declared earlier (for example Tailwind's preflight in `@layer base`)\ndo not leak into rows. Rules in later layers or unlayered rules still win.\nImport `solid-trees/styles.css` after your reset, or declare the order up front:"},"608":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#42","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#color-scheme","content":"The root sets `color-scheme: light dark`, so colors follow the OS preference.\nPin it with `style={{ 'color-scheme': 'dark' }}` or CSS."},"609":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#43","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#page-css-escape-hatch","content":"The tree renders into the light DOM, so page CSS reaches it. It replaces\nupstream's `unsafeCSS`. Use it only when the supported host and variable\nsurfaces cannot express the customization."},"610":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#44","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#page-css-escape-hatch","content":"The DOM keeps upstream's data attributes (`data-type=\"item\"`, `data-item-path`,\n`data-item-selected`, `data-item-focused`, `data-item-git-status`,\n`data-item-section`, `data-file-tree-sticky-row`, ...), so upstream CSS ports\nover. The focused row's parent indent guide carries\n`data-item-guide-focused=\"true\"`."},"611":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#45","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#page-css-escape-hatch","content":"Keep it narrow. Do not rebuild the visual system from raw selectors."},"612":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#46","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#related-pages","content":"Style and theme the tree for the\nwalkthrough"},"613":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#47","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#related-pages","content":"Icons for icon-specific configuration"},"614":{"id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#48","page_id":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/styling-and-theming#related-pages","content":"Show Git status and row annotations\nfor signal meaning"}},"count":614},"sorting":{"language":"english","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":200,"2":269,"3":395,"4":376,"5":351,"6":350,"7":256,"8":228,"9":241,"10":202,"11":484,"12":188,"13":587,"14":434,"15":579,"16":485,"17":132,"18":81,"19":139,