rk without\nthe stylesheet."],[605,"`solid-trees.theme` is reserved for your theme rules."],[434,"`solid-trees` accepts three related input shapes:"],[84,"`solid-trees` already virtualizes the visible row window. Most apps do not need\ncustom virtualization primitives."],[121,"`solid-trees` also supports `collapse-non-matches` and `expand-matches`. Use\nthose modes when the surrounding UI needs more context. But keep\n`hide-non-matches` as the default mental model. The shared meaning of all three\nmodes is in\nShared concepts."],[166,"`solid-trees` emits path-based rename and drop events. Your app decides whether\nto save those changes. It can save them to a server, local state, or another\nboundary. Keep this separation clear."],[494,"`solid-trees` exposes semantic tree mutations, not DOM events. The shared\nmutation terms are:"],[48,"`solid-trees` gives you one path-first model and a thin Solid layer over it:\n`createFileTree(...)` creates the model, and `<FileTree model={...} />` renders\nit. The primitives `createFileTreeSelection(...)`, `createFileTreeSearch(...)`,\nand `createFileTreeSelector(...)` derive reactive values from the same model."],[17,"`solid-trees` includes three built-in sets:"],[588,"`solid-trees` resolves styling in this order:"],[201,"`solid-trees` supports these built-in statuses:"],[472,"`solid-trees` supports three search modes:"],[265,"`solid-trees` vendors upstream's model layer (path store, controller, focus,\nselection, search, rename, drag and drop, Git status). The view is a native\nSolid 2 rewrite of upstream's Preact `FileTreeView`, rendered into the light\nDOM, with upstream's visual styles shipped as an importable stylesheet."],[298,"`spriteSheet?: string`"],[288,"`standard` adds common language and file-type icons"],[19,"`standard` for common language and file-type recognition"],[380,"`startRenaming(path?)`"],[570,"`themeToTreeStyles(...)`"],[247,"`themeToTreeStyles(...)` when the tree must inherit an editor palette"],[593,"`the